{"id":"mahabharata-2-058","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":58,"title":"अष्टपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 58 · Yudhishthira stakes his brothers, himself and Draupadi","summary":{"en":"Having lost all his wealth, Yudhishthira stakes Nakula, Sahadeva, Arjuna and Bhima one by one, then himself, and loses each. Shakuni taunts him that he still has Draupadi, and Yudhishthira, praising her beauty, stakes her; amid cries of horror Shakuni wins.","kn":"ಸಂಪತ್ತೆಲ್ಲ ಸೋತ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ನಕುಲ, ಸಹದೇವ, ಅರ್ಜುನ, ಭೀಮರನ್ನು ಒಬ್ಬೊಬ್ಬರಾಗಿ, ಅನಂತರ ತನ್ನನ್ನೇ ಪಣವಿಟ್ಟು ಸೋಲುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇನ್ನೂ ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಇದ್ದಾಳೆ ಎಂದು ಶಕುನಿ ಹಂಗಿಸಿದಾಗ ಅವಳ ಸೌಂದರ್ಯವನ್ನು ಹೊಗಳಿ ಅವಳನ್ನೂ ಪಣವಿಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭಯಾಕ್ರಂದನಗಳ ನಡುವೆ ಶಕುನಿ ಗೆಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सारा धन हारकर युधिष्ठिर नकुल, सहदेव, अर्जुन और भीम को एक-एक कर, फिर स्वयं को दाँव पर लगाते हैं और हर बार हारते हैं। शकुनि ताना देता है कि अभी द्रौपदी शेष है, और युधिष्ठिर उनके सौन्दर्य की प्रशंसा करते हुए उन्हें दाँव पर लगाते हैं; हाहाकार के बीच शकुनि जीत जाता है।","te":"సంపదంతా ఓడిన యుధిష్ఠిరుడు నకులుని, సహదేవుని, అర్జునుని, భీముని ఒక్కొక్కరిగా, తర్వాత తనను తానే పణంగా పెట్టి ఓడిపోతాడు. ఇంకా ద్రౌపది ఉంది కదా అని శకుని ఎత్తిపొడవగా ఆమె సౌందర్యాన్ని పొగుడుతూ ఆమెనూ పణంగా పెడతాడు; హాహాకారాల మధ్య శకుని గెలుస్తాడు.","ta":"செல்வம் அனைத்தையும் இழந்த யுதிஷ்டிரர் நகுலன், ஸஹதேவன், அர்ஜுனன், பீமன் ஆகியோரை ஒவ்வொருவராக, பின்னர் தம்மையே பந்தயம் வைத்துத் தோற்கிறார். இன்னும் திரௌபதி இருக்கிறாளே என்று ஶகுனி ஏளனம் செய்ய, அவள் அழகைப் புகழ்ந்து அவளையும் பந்தயம் வைக்கிறார்; அலறல்களிடையே ஶகுனி வெல்கிறான்.","ml":"സമ്പത്ത് മുഴുവൻ നഷ്ടപ്പെട്ട യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ നകുലനെയും സഹദേവനെയും അർജുനനെയും ഭീമനെയും ഓരോരുത്തരെയായി പണയം വെക്കുന്നു, പിന്നെ തന്നെത്തന്നെയും; ഓരോന്നും നഷ്ടപ്പെടുന്നു. ഇനി ദ്രൗപദി ഉണ്ടല്ലോ എന്ന് ശകുനി പരിഹസിക്കുന്നു; അവളുടെ സൗന്ദര്യത്തെ പുകഴ്ത്തിക്കൊണ്ട് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ അവളെയും പണയം വെക്കുന്നു; ഭീതിയുടെ നിലവിളികൾക്കിടയിൽ ശകുനി ജയിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.58; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"द्यूतपर्व","titleEn":"Dyuta Parva (The dice game)","verses":[{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"बहु वित्तं पराजैषीः पाण्डवानां युधिष्ठिर ।\nआचक्ष्व वित्तं कौन्तेय यदि तेऽस्त्यपराजितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, you have lost a great deal of the Pandavas' wealth. Tell me, son of Kunti, if you still have any wealth that has not been lost."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"मम वित्तमसंख्येयं यदहं वेद सौबल ।\nअथ त्वं शकुने कस्माद्वित्तं समनुपृच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Subala, my wealth is beyond counting, as far as I know it. Why do you ask me about wealth, Shakuni?"}},{"n":3,"text":"अयुतं प्रयुतं चैव खर्वं पद्मं तथार्बुदम् ।\nशङ्खं चैव निखर्वं च समुद्रं चात्र पण्यताम् ।\nएतन्मम धनं राजंस्तेन दीव्याम्यहं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ten thousands, hundred thousands, a hundred million, ten billion, and so on up to the numbers called shankha, nikharva and samudra: put these up as stake. This is my wealth, king; I play against you with it."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा व्यवसितो निकृतिं समुपाश्रितः ।\nजितमित्येव शकुनिर्युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, resolved and relying on cheating, Shakuni said to Yudhishthira, I have won."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"गवाश्वं बहुधेनूकमसंख्येयमजाविकम् ।\nयत्किंचिदनुवर्णानां प्राक्सिन्धोरपि सौबल ।\nएतन्मम धनं राजंस्तेन दीव्याम्यहं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cattle and horses, many milch cows, uncountable goats and sheep, and whatever there is among the castes east of the Sindhu, Shakuni: this is my wealth, king; I play against you with it."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा व्यवसितो निकृतिं समुपाश्रितः ।\nजितमित्येव शकुनिर्युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, resolved and relying on cheating, Shakuni said to Yudhishthira, I have won."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"पुरं जनपदो भूमिरब्राह्मणधनैः सह ।\nअब्राह्मणाश्च पुरुषा राजञ्शिष्टं धनं मम ।\nएतद्राजन्धनं मह्यं तेन दीव्याम्यहं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"My city, my country, and the land, together with all wealth other than the brahmins' property, and all men other than brahmins, king, is my remaining wealth. This is my wealth; I play against you with it."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा व्यवसितो निकृतिं समुपाश्रितः ।\nजितमित्येव शकुनिर्युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, resolved and relying on cheating, Shakuni said to Yudhishthira, I have won."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"राजपुत्रा इमे राजञ्शोभन्ते येन भूषिताः ।\nकुण्डलानि च निष्काश्च सर्वं चाङ्गविभूषणम् ।\nएतन्मम धनं राजंस्तेन दीव्याम्यहं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"These princes, king, shine with the ornaments they wear: their earrings, necklaces and all adornments of the body. This is my wealth, king; I play against you with it."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा व्यवसितो निकृतिं समुपाश्रितः ।\nजितमित्येव शकुनिर्युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, resolved and relying on cheating, Shakuni said to Yudhishthira, I have won."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"श्यामो युवा लोहिताक्षः सिंहस्कन्धो महाभुजः ।\nनकुलो ग्लह एको मे यच्चैतत्स्वगतं धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula, dark, young, red-eyed, lion-shouldered and long-armed, is my one stake, together with the rest of my own wealth."}},{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"प्रियस्ते नकुलो राजन्राजपुत्रो युधिष्ठिर ।\nअस्माकं धनतां प्राप्तो भूयस्त्वं केन दीव्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Yudhishthira, Nakula is dear to you, a prince; he has now become our wealth. With what will you gamble further?"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा तु शकुनिस्तानक्षान्प्रत्यपद्यत ।\nजितमित्येव शकुनिर्युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, Shakuni took up the dice, and then said to Yudhishthira, I have won."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"अयं धर्मान्सहदेवोऽनुशास्ति\nलोके ह्यस्मिन्पण्डिताख्यां गतश्च ।\nअनर्हता राजपुत्रेण तेन\nत्वया दीव्याम्यप्रियवत्प्रियेण ॥","meaning":{"en":"This Sahadeva teaches dharma and has won the name of scholar in this world. Though he does not deserve it, a prince, I stake him against you, as if he were unloved though he is dear."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा व्यवसितो निकृतिं समुपाश्रितः ।\nजितमित्येव शकुनिर्युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, resolved and relying on cheating, Shakuni said to Yudhishthira, I have won."}},{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"माद्रीपुत्रौ प्रियौ राजंस्तवेमौ विजितौ मया ।\nगरीयांसौ तु ते मन्ये भीमसेनधनंजयौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two sons of Madri, dear to you, king, have been won by me. But I think Bhimasena and Arjuna are weightier for you."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"अधर्मं चरसे नूनं यो नावेक्षसि वै नयम् ।\nयो नः सुमनसां मूढ विभेदं कर्तुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely you act unrighteously, since you do not look to proper conduct, you fool, wishing to divide us who are of one mind."}},{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"गर्ते मत्तः प्रपतति प्रमत्तः स्थाणुमृच्छति ।\nज्येष्ठो राजन्वरिष्ठोऽसि नमस्ते भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"A drunk man falls into a pit; a careless one runs into a stump. King, you are elder and the best; I bow to you, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":19,"text":"स्वप्ने न तानि पश्यन्ति जाग्रतो वा युधिष्ठिर ।\nकितवा यानि दीव्यन्तः प्रलपन्त्युत्कटा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gamblers, Yudhishthira, do not see in dream or in waking those things that they babble as they play, as if mad."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"यो नः संख्ये नौरिव पारनेता\nजेता रिपूणां राजपुत्रस्तरस्वी ।\nअनर्हता लोकवीरेण तेन\nदीव्याम्यहं शकुने फल्गुनेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who in battle carries us across like a boat, the victor over enemies, the mighty prince: though that world-hero does not deserve it, I gamble with Phalguna, Shakuni."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा व्यवसितो निकृतिं समुपाश्रितः ।\nजितमित्येव शकुनिर्युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, resolved and relying on cheating, Shakuni said to Yudhishthira, I have won."}},{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"अयं मया पाण्डवानां धनुर्धरः\nपराजितः पाण्डवः सव्यसाची ।\nभीमेन राजन्दयितेन दीव्य\nयत्कैतव्यं पाण्डव तेऽवशिष्टम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have won this archer of the Pandavas, Pandava Savyasachin. Gamble now with Bhima, dear to you, king: whatever of your stake remains."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"यो नो नेता यो युधां नः प्रणेता\nयथा वज्री दानवशत्रुरेकः ।\nतिर्यक्प्रेक्षी संहतभ्रूर्महात्मा\nसिंहस्कन्धो यश्च सदात्यमर्षी ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who is our leader, who leads us in fights, like the single wielder of the thunderbolt, enemy of the Danavas, great-souled, who looks sidelong, with knit brows, lion-shouldered and always impatient,"}},{"n":24,"text":"बलेन तुल्यो यस्य पुमान्न विद्यते\nगदाभृतामग्र्य इहारिमर्दनः ।\nअनर्हता राजपुत्रेण तेन\nदीव्याम्यहं भीमसेनेन राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whose equal in strength is not found, foremost of mace-bearers here, crusher of foes: though that prince does not deserve it, I gamble with Bhimasena, king."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा व्यवसितो निकृतिं समुपाश्रितः ।\nजितमित्येव शकुनिर्युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, resolved and relying on cheating, Shakuni said to Yudhishthira, I have won."}},{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"बहु वित्तं पराजैषीर्भ्रातॄंश्च सहयद्विपान् ।\nआचक्ष्व वित्तं कौन्तेय यदि तेऽस्त्यपराजितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have lost much wealth and your brothers with horses and elephants. Tell me, son of Kunti, if you have any wealth not yet lost."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"अहं विशिष्टः सर्वेषां भ्रातॄणां दयितस्तथा ।\nकुर्यामस्ते जिताः कर्म स्वयमात्मन्युपप्लवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am the most special of all my brothers and dear to them. If I am won, we who are lost will do service ourselves, in our own downfall."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":28,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा व्यवसितो निकृतिं समुपाश्रितः ।\nजितमित्येव शकुनिर्युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, resolved and relying on cheating, Shakuni said to Yudhishthira, I have won."}},{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":29,"text":"एतत्पापिष्ठमकरोर्यदात्मानं पराजितः ।\nशिष्टे सति धने राजन्पाप आत्मपराजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You did the worst of things by losing yourself. King, when other wealth remains, losing oneself is a sin."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":30,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा मताक्षस्तान्ग्लहे सर्वानवस्थितान् ।\nपराजयल्लोकवीरानाक्षेपेण पृथक्पृथक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So saying, Shakuni, skilled at dice, staked them all, one by one, and defeated those world-heroes with taunts."}},{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"अस्ति वै ते प्रिया देवी ग्लह एकोऽपराजितः ।\nपणस्व कृष्णां पाञ्चालीं तयात्मानं पुनर्जय ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have a dear queen, the one stake not yet lost. Stake Krishna, the Panchali, and win yourself back with her."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"नैव ह्रस्वा न महती नातिकृष्णा न रोहिणी ।\nसरागरक्तनेत्रा च तया दीव्याम्यहं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"She is neither short nor tall, neither too dark nor reddish, with eyes red with passion. I play against you with her."}},{"n":33,"text":"शारदोत्पलपत्राक्ष्या शारदोत्पलगन्धया ।\nशारदोत्पलसेविन्या रूपेण श्रीसमानया ॥","meaning":{"en":"With eyes like autumn lotus petals, fragrant as the autumn lotus, who delights in autumn lotuses, equal to Shri in beauty,"}},{"n":34,"text":"तथैव स्यादानृशंस्यात्तथा स्याद्रूपसंपदा ।\nतथा स्याच्छीलसंपत्त्या यामिच्छेत्पुरुषः स्त्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who is as one would wish a woman to be, in gentleness, in wealth of beauty, and in richness of character,"}},{"n":35,"text":"चरमं संविशति या प्रथमं प्रतिबुध्यते ।\nआ गोपालाविपालेभ्यः सर्वं वेद कृताकृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who goes to bed last and wakes first, and knows what has and has not been done, down to the herdsmen and shepherds,"}},{"n":36,"text":"आभाति पद्मवद्वक्त्रं सस्वेदं मल्लिकेव च ।\nवेदीमध्या दीर्घकेशी ताम्राक्षी नातिरोमशा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose face shines like a lotus and, sweating, like jasmine; who rose from the middle of the altar, long-haired, copper-eyed, not too hairy,"}},{"n":37,"text":"तयैवंविधया राजन्पाञ्चाल्याहं सुमध्यया ।\nग्लहं दीव्यामि चार्वङ्ग्या द्रौपद्या हन्त सौबल ॥","meaning":{"en":"With such a Panchali, slender-waisted and lovely-limbed, Draupadi, I stake her in play against you, Shakuni."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":38,"text":"एवमुक्ते तु वचने धर्मराजेन भारत ।\nधिग्धिगित्येव वृद्धानां सभ्यानां निःसृता गिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the king of dharma had said this, cries of Shame! Shame! came out from the elders in the assembly, Bharata."}},{"n":39,"text":"चुक्षुभे सा सभा राजन्राज्ञां संजज्ञिरे कथाः ।\nभीष्मद्रोणकृपादीनां स्वेदश्च समजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hall was shaken, king; talk arose among the kings; and sweat broke out on Bhishma, Drona, Kripa and the others."}},{"n":40,"text":"शिरो गृहीत्वा विदुरो गतसत्त्व इवाभवत् ।\nआस्ते ध्यायन्नधोवक्त्रो निःश्वसन्पन्नगो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vidura, holding his head, seemed lifeless; he sat thinking, face down, sighing like a snake."}},{"n":41,"text":"धृतराष्ट्रस्तु संहृष्टः पर्यपृच्छत्पुनः पुनः ।\nकिं जितं किं जितमिति ह्याकारं नाभ्यरक्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Dhritarashtra, delighted, asked again and again, What was won? What was won? and could not hide his expression."}},{"n":42,"text":"जहर्ष कर्णोऽतिभृशं सह दुःशासनादिभिः ।\nइतरेषां तु सभ्यानां नेत्रेभ्यः प्रापतज्जलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna rejoiced greatly with Duhshasana and the others, but from the eyes of the other assembly members tears fell."}},{"n":43,"text":"सौबलस्त्वविचार्यैव जितकाशी मदोत्कटः ।\nजितमित्येव तानक्षान्पुनरेवान्वपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Subala's son, intoxicated, not stopping to think, having won, again took up the dice saying, I have won."}}]}]}